<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6881" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Carrīnas</span></b> , ātis,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a Roman proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Secundus, <i>a
				rhetorician</i>, <i>sent under Nero to
			Achaia</i>, <i>and expelled from Rome by
			Caligula</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 15, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 7,
			204</span></i>; <i>died by poison</i>, Schol. Juv. ad
			loc.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> T.
			Carrinas, <i>the name of a bore mentioned by</i>
			<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Att. 13, 33, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
